# A sheet of eight shipping labels for A4 label paper, two columns of four labels of 99.1 × 67.7 mm: a Grid with
# fixed column and row sizes, and the margins of the sheet in Page. Each label has the service written vertically in
# a coloured band (a Text with Rotate: -90, which takes the rectangle of the rotated text, centred in a vertical
# Stack), the sender, the recipient, a GS1-128 barcode with the SSCC of the parcel and its readable text, and a Data
# Matrix with the routing code for the sorting machines. The name of the recipient has a fixed height and Overflow:
# shrink, so a long name gets smaller, on two lines, instead of pushing the barcode out of the label (the allotment
# association on the third and fourth labels). The dotted outline of each label is for checking the sheet on screen;
# it falls on the cuts of the paper.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
